„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ£Jesus answered, Thou couldest have no power at all against me, except it were given thee from above: therefore he that delivered me unto thee hath the greater sin.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÂAnd from thenceforth Pilate sought to release him: but the Jews cried out, saying, If thou let this man go, thou art not CÃ¦sar's friend: whosoever maketh himself a king speaketh against CÃ¦sar.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§When Pilate therefore heard that saying, he brought Jesus forth, and sat down in the judgment seat in a place that is called the Pavement, but in the Hebrew, Gabbatha.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsAnd it was the preparation of the passover, and about the sixth hour: and he saith unto the Jews, Behold your King!¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ©But they cried out, Away with him, away with him, crucify him. Pilate saith unto them, Shall I crucify your King? The chief priests answered, We have no king but CÃ¦sar.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ:Then delivered he him therefore unto them to be crucified.¦layout ‚¤textÙ&And they took Jesus, and led him away.¦layout©paragraphªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙuAnd he bearing his cross went forth into a place called the place of a skull, which is called in the Hebrew Golgotha:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]where they crucified him, and two other with him, on either side one, and Jesus in the midst.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoAnd Pilate wrote a title, and put it on the cross. And the writing was, JESUS OF NAZARETH THE KING OF THE JEWS.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ˜This title then read many of the Jews: for the place where Jesus was crucified was nigh to the city: and it was written in Hebrew, and Greek, and Latin.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|Then said the chief priests of the Jews to Pilate, Write not, The King of the Jews; but that he said, I am King of the Jews.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ4Pilate answered, What I have written I have written.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÃThen the soldiers, when they had crucified Jesus, took his garments, and made four parts, to every soldier a part; and also his coat: now the coat was without seam, woven from the top throughout.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ	They said therefore among themselves, Let us not rend it, but cast lots for it, whose it shall be: that the scripture might be fulfilled, which saith, They parted my raiment among them, and for my vesture they did cast lots. These things therefore the soldiers did.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyNow there stood by the cross of Jesus his mother, and his mother's sister, Mary the wife of Cleophas, and Mary Magdalene.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚When Jesus therefore saw his mother, and the disciple standing by, whom he loved, he saith unto his mother, Woman, behold thy son!¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnThen saith he to the disciple, Behold thy mother! And from that hour that disciple took her unto his own home.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxAfter this, Jesus knowing that all things were now accomplished, that the scripture might be fulfilled, saith, I thirst.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒNow there was set a vessel full of vinegar: and they filled a spunge with vinegar, and put it upon hyssop, and put it to his mouth.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙuWhen Jesus therefore had received the vinegar, he said, It is finished: and he bowed his head, and gave up the ghost.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse%¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙôThe Jews therefore, because it was the preparation, that the bodies should not remain upon the cross on the sabbath day, (for that sabbath day was an high day,) besought Pilate that their legs might be broken, and that they might be taken away.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙgThen came the soldiers, and brake the legs of the first, and of the other which was crucified with him.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWBut when they came to Jesus, and saw that he was dead already, they brake not his legs:¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdbut one of the soldiers with a spear pierced his side, and forthwith came there out blood and water.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqAnd he that saw it bare record, and his record is true: and he knoweth that he saith true, that ye might believe.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙfFor these things were done, that the scripture should be fulfilled, A bone of him shall not be broken.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙLAnd again another scripture saith, They shall look on him whom they pierced.¦layout ªlast_verse%…¤book*§chapter«first_verse&ªlast_verse*¦verses•„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙçAnd after this Joseph of ArimathÃ¦a, being a disciple of Jesus, but secretly for fear of the Jews, besought Pilate that he might take away the body of Jesus: and Pilate gave him leave. He came therefore, and took the body of Jesus.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’And there came also Nicodemus, which at the first came to Jesus by night, and brought a mixture of myrrh and aloes, about an hundred pound weight.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvThen took they the body of Jesus, and wound it in linen clothes with the spices, as the manner of the Jews is to bury.¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~Now in the place where he was crucified there was a garden; and in the garden a new sepulchre, wherein was never man yet laid.¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙiThere laid they Jesus therefore because of the Jews' preparation day; for the sepulchre was nigh at hand.¦layout ªlast_verse*